Authored arnold:global:color_space_linear overrides renderingColorSpace with Hydra 2

The render settings prim of with_global.usda authors renderingColorSpace = "lin_b" and
arnold:global:color_space_linear = "lin_a". As in the usd procedural, the arnold attribute must win, so
the color manager gets "lin_a" in every pass. Before the fix, the Hydra 2 render settings prim dropped
arnold:global:color_space_linear as an unknown option, and "lin_b" was used. without_global.usda only
authors renderingColorSpace, which must then be used.

See ARNOLD-18814

author: sebastien.blaineau.ortega@autodesk.com

PARAMS: {}
